Based on the verified temporal evidence for the relevant date of 17 June 1951, clause (2) of Article 174 provided that, subject to the provisions of clause (1), the Governor may from time to time:

(a) summon the House or either House to meet at such time and place as he thinks fit;  
(b) prorogue the House or Houses;  
(c) dissolve the Legislative Assembly.

Based on the verified evidence for Article 174 as of 1 May 2026, under clause (2), the Governor may from time to time:
(a) prorogue the House or either House;
(b) dissolve the Legislative Assembly.
